# Next.js Code Review

Review Next.js frontend changes across five dimensions. Only report findings that apply; skip empty sections. For each finding: file/line, issue, why it matters, concrete fix. End with Critical / Should Fix / Nice to Have.

This app uses the **App Router** under `client/src/app/`.

## 1. Code Standards

- Typed props and API responses; no unnecessary `any`.
- `"use client"` only where needed (state, effects, browser APIs, handlers); keep client boundaries as leaves.
- Follow `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx` conventions; PascalCase components; `useX` hooks.
- HTTP only via `client/src/lib/api/` + shared `axios` instance — not ad hoc `fetch` in pages.
- **Enums:** roles, statuses, auth error/redirect codes live in `client/src/types/` as string enums matching the server. No scattered `'ADMIN'` / `'SUPERADMIN'` / status literals in components or route helpers.

## 2. Reusable Components

- Shared UI in `client/src/components/`; reusable hooks in `client/src/hooks/`.
- Prefer layout composition and providers over copy-pasted headers/gates per page.
- Centralize design tokens (Tailwind / CSS variables); avoid one-off magic colors/spacing when a token exists.

## 3. Security

- No secrets in client code or `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` unless safe to expose.
- Auth redirects and `RoleGate` are UX only — real authorization is on the API. Do not treat client role checks as security.
- Avoid `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` unless sanitized; validate external URLs before rendering links/images.
- Do not store tokens in places that leak to XSS beyond the existing auth pattern; never log access tokens.

## 4. Performance

- Prefer Server Components for data-heavy shells; dynamic-import heavy client-only UI.
- Parallelize independent requests; avoid fetch waterfalls in hooks.
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` / `React.memo` by default — only when profiling or existing code already uses them (align with React Compiler guidance).
- Use `next/image` and `next/font` where images/fonts are introduced.

## 5. Architecture

- Types in `client/src/types/` stay aligned with server DTOs/interfaces/enums.
- Route groups and role-based pages (`superadmin/`, settings) must use shared auth helpers (`auth-routes`, gates) consistently.
- Error/empty/loading states handled per route; keep business rules on the server.
